\details{
DupCaller inputs must be completed call and estimate outputs from version 1.2.11 or newer using its 192-row SBS opportunity table and 23-column coverage BED. Files are read from SBS/, INDEL/ and DBS/ subdirectories, with stats, coverage and parameter logs at the sample root. Older formats are not supported.

For DupCaller, background tables use 96 substitution labels (e.g. ACA>AAA), preserving alternate-specific effective opportunities after reverse-complement folding. Dividing their sum by three gives SBS base coverage. Reference contexts are repeated for their three possible alternate bases. Zero-opportunity channels contribute zero corrected mutations, matching DupCaller. Corrected SBS confidence intervals use the Fay-Feuer weighted gamma method; rates with zero base coverage are undefined.

DupCaller indel base coverage comes from the estimate stats. Excluded coverage is expanded from the 16 BED channels to ID83 opportunity multiplicities, then divided by the run's reference indel opportunity multiplier (ID83 reference opportunities / reference bases). This fixed multiplier also normalizes regional results, so coverage remains additive across regions. Indel spectra continue to use the package's indelwald classifier.

DupCaller mutation_burden additionally contains dbs_observed and dbs_unique_observed event counts. DBS burdens and spectra are not calculated.
